{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YGU57uPUFh14SQXtVUh85i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims about what it is and ships:\n\n- **It's a single-folder, stdlib-only productivity app** living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no OneDrive/syncing). Markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`, etc.) are the source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **The main interface is `anchor_gui.py`** â€” a self-contained Python HTTP server (Python stdlib only) that generates the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes directly back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` bound to `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) exposes the same logic and also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core productivity surface:** task lifecycle management (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored), quick-capture inbox, per-domain views (academic, commercial, family, writing), priorities/energy/due-dates, and daily activity logs â€” all editable live in the browser.\n\n- **It has grown a layered \"R&D control surface\" (v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4)** that turns each project into a cockpit for \"trio\"-driven development (Research â†’ Planning â†’ Build, mapped to the researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman skills). This ships: session-grouped history, cached & grounded auto-summaries, a Grass-Catchers idea lane, and pinned/declared deliverables.\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\" added real server-side terminals:** ConPTY-backed interactive sessions (the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, optional and lazily imported), per-session git-worktree isolation, a durable session registry, stage handoffs between planâ†’build, and a guarded ephemeral deliverable-preview server (always on a free port â‰  8777).\n\n- **v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (built + merged 2026-06-13) is the current shape:** each lane is a tile with one honest status light; clicking expands an inline panel (balanced summary on top, resizable xterm.js terminal below) instead of navigating away. A new session auto-loads the lane's skill exactly once and greets once (fixing the old repeating-prompt bug), supports a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc-role links, a project cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **It ships its own reliability tooling:** a daily 5 AM health-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (never touching the live service or real data), writing dated reports under `health_reports/`; plus Ghost World Labs branding (\"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\") and a deny-by-default distribution builder (`distro.py`) that enforces the stdlib-only-plus-one-exception rule."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f2887c7-32eb-45e6-9842-ce3c81528ebd","uuid":"e3df0c61-ad3a-4ec0-bebe-6164ab0af442","request_id":"req_011Cc2MPoV94sBkxM3vAFNL6"}
